  "generated_text": "To solve this problem, we need to use the formula for compound interest:\n\\[ A = P(1 + r)^n \\]\nwhere $A$ is the amount of money accumulated after $n$ years, including interest, $P$ is the principal amount, $r$ is the annual interest rate, and $n$ is the number of years.\n\nIn this case, $P = 1000$, $r = 0.01$, and $n = 5$. Plugging these values into the formula, we get:\n\\[ A = 1000(1 + 0.01)^5 \\]\n\\[ A = 1000(1.01)^5 \\]\n\\[ A = 1000(1.05101) \\]\n\\[ A = 1051.01 \\]\n\nSince we want to find the interest earned, we subtract the principal amount from the total amount:\n\\[ \\text{Interest} = A - P \\]\n\\[ \\text{Interest} = 1051.01 - 1000 \\]\n\\[ \\text{Interest} = \\boxed{51} \\text{ dollars}\\]",
